{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And I will make all my mountains a way.</b> That the mountains will be lowered and the highways raised, and so they are in a valley." "And the word <b>ירומון</b> comes with highways as in אם תמצאו את דודי (Song of Songs 5:8). But the main point is otherwise: since all is plural language, they do not object to saying masculine forms for feminine. And some say that the sense of כל הרי is that the captives will be so numerous that they walk upon the mountains, and they interpret ירומון as referring to the captives, as if it were ועל מסלותי ירומון."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "Verse citation Song of Songs 5:8 given as ט' ח' (9:8) in the Hebrew; correct chapter-verse is 5:8, presumably a corruption or chapter miscount."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:44.886408786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}